  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1105 AM CST Tue Nov 10 2026\n\nA cold front remains on track to move through the area tomorrow,\nbringing a period of below normal temperatures and for Wednesday, gusty\nnortherly winds. A dry cold frontal passage remains expected. The\ngusty winds and drop in dew points on Wednesday behind the front \nwill bring a period of limited fire spread conditions, particularly\nto parts of northeast Oklahoma. Winds will pick up to some extent\nonce again on Thursday afternoon across southeast Oklahoma and\nwestern Arkansas but the corresponding fire spread concerns\ncurrently appears below that of Wednesday.\n\nSurface high pressure will nose into the area Thursday night into\nFriday, dropping Friday morning lows into the low to mid 30s\nacross a good portion of northeast Oklahoma and northwest\nArkansas. Will not include frost in the forecast for now, but\ngiven the forecast humidities and winds, this will likely be\nneeded. Frost/Freeze headlines should be expected as well. The\nchilly temperatures will extend into Friday and Friday night, with\nanother round of Frost/Freeze headlines possible into Saturday\nmorning. \n\nThe surface high will shift east of the area on Saturday, with\nsoutherly winds and warmer temperatures returning. An upper level\ntrough remains on track to move through the region Sunday,\npossibly extending into early Monday, bringing the next chance of\nrain to the area. Dry weather and seasonable temperatures will\nfollow the departure of the trough Monday into Tuesday.",
